    <td valign="top"><font face="Trebuchet MS, Arial, Helvetica"> <span class="Heading">Recruiting</span> 
      <p><font face="Verdana,Arial" size="2">Dusk Eternal is a a close knit guild, 
        but also one based upon freedom and comradery, rather than harsh rules 
        and stringent guidelines.&nbsp; As a result, our recruiting policy is 
        pretty informal.&nbsp; However, under it all lies the central spirit of 
        the guild, we must all get along and we must all be able to work and contribute 
        as a team.<br>
        <br>
        The policy is as follows:<br>
        Anyone can sponsor someone to be a member of the guild. Although it would 
        be preferred that people only sponsor one prospect at a time, this is 
        not a hard fast rule. Simply tell the guild either in Guild Chat or on 
        the message board that they want to sponsor this person. That person will 
        be invited along on the next &quot;event&quot; that is close to their 
        level. After the event all Dusk Eternal members will be asked to vote. 
        If the majority approve, they get an invite. If not, we wait.<br>
        <br>
        Note: If the event is a raid, we may limit it to 2-3 new recruits. Having 
        too many new people can really effect raids.&nbsp; It is important that 
        we not only get a chance to know these people, and work with them, but 
        for us to demonstrate our skills and organization. Joining a guild should 
        be something everyone is interested in.<br>
        <br>
        For those that have higher level alts, that are sort of &quot;alone&quot; 
        until there are multiple people of similar level, we will simply trust 
        your judgment for the first invite. Any after then should be approved 
        by both similarly leveled members.<br>
        </font> 
      </font> 
      <!--msnavigation-->
